@startuml
title Singleton Pattern - StoreConfiguration (SOLID analysis)

skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam shadowing false

package "Singleton" {
  class StoreConfiguration <<singleton>> {
    - _instance : Lazy<StoreConfiguration>
    - StoreConfiguration()
    + Instance : StoreConfiguration
    + StoreName : string
    + TaxRate : decimal
    + Currency : string
    + Configure(name : string, tax : decimal, currency : string) : void
  }
}

package "Client" {
  class Program {
    + Main() : void
  }
}

Program --> StoreConfiguration : directly uses\nStoreConfiguration.Instance



note bottom of StoreConfiguration
SOLID observations:
S - Violated:
  handles both business state
  and its own instantiation

O - Violated:
  private constructor blocks extension

L - Violated:
  cannot be substituted by subclasses

I - Respected:
  compact public interface

D - Violated:
  client depends directly on
  StoreConfiguration.Instance
end note
@enduml